WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.010
There's honestly nothing more satisfying

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:04.270
than a good poop.

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:07.780
On the flip side, a bad
poop can ruin your day.

00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:09.534
You know what I'm talking about.

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:13.620
Too hard, too soft, too
sudden, not soon enough.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:15.768
If this isn't ringing any bells,

00:00:15.768 --> 00:00:19.060
congrats on being the
world's only perfect pooper!

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:21.550
A title to wear with pride.

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:24.640
For the rest of us, we have to work at it.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.600
The good news is we have
science on our side.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.230
There are a bunch of things we can do

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:31.970
to smooth out the kinks
in our digestive system,

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:33.695
and some of them are very literal.

00:00:33.695 --> 00:00:35.386
But real quick, let us introduce you

00:00:35.386 --> 00:00:38.270
to the Bristol stool
scale, a handy-dandy chart

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:41.478
listing the different types
of poop your body can make.

00:00:41.478 --> 00:00:44.010
They range from type one, hard lumps,

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.490
to type seven, totally liquid.

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:47.680
When it comes to No. 2,

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:50.340
you actually want to be
a type three or four.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:53.170
Anything before indicates constipation;

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:55.920
anything after gets closer to diarrhea.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:57.500
Depending on where you land on the scale,

00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:59.150
there are a number of things you can do

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:02.290
to get that coveted smooth snake.

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:04.203
Let's start with short-term solutions.

00:01:04.203 --> 00:01:06.990
[mooing]

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:09.550
Mooing like a cow, or
making a similar noise

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:12.002
if you aren't feeling particularly bovine,

00:01:12.002 --> 00:01:13.810
can help reduce straining.

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:14.950
You'll want to lean forward

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:17.207
with your elbows on your
knees while you do it.

00:01:17.207 --> 00:01:19.090
The idea is to open up your belly

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:22.472
and get yourself in a more
efficient pooping position.

00:01:22.472 --> 00:01:25.610
You see, sitting toilets
were designed all wrong.

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:27.853
Sitting straight up with your
feet planted on the ground

00:01:27.853 --> 00:01:30.200
actually makes it harder
to squeeze one out.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:32.130
Too much straining and pushing

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:34.300
can lead to hemorrhoids, most of all,

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:36.447
but sometimes even prolapse.

00:01:36.447 --> 00:01:38.000
Thanks to how our bodies are built,

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:39.510
we're better off in a squat.

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:40.770
It's all in the gut.

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:43.750
Look at the angle of her
rectum when she stands up.

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:45.465
It's bent at about 80 degrees

00:01:45.465 --> 00:01:47.420
right where it meets the anal canal,

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:49.970
fittingly named the anorectal angle.

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:51.490
Sort of like kinking a hose,

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:53.540
this bend helps you control your bowels,

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:55.840
along with the muscles in the same area.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:59.320
When you sit, that angle
unfolds to about 100 degrees,

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:01.560
and squatting opens it even further.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:03.650
Opening up that pathway makes it easier

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:05.800
for stuff to slide on through.

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:07.430
But even though our porcelain thrones

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:10.280
aren't suited for squatting,
there are ways to adapt.

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:11.980
You can throw your feet up on a stool

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:14.757
or even just a couple of
rolls of toilet paper.

00:02:14.757 --> 00:02:16.572
Or the dedicated can buy a product

00:02:16.572 --> 00:02:18.804
specifically made for this purpose,

00:02:18.804 --> 00:02:22.000
like the Squatty Potty
or Nature's Platform.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.656
One study followed over 50 healthy poopers

00:02:24.656 --> 00:02:26.980
through 1,000 collective bowel movements

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.450
using the Squatty Potty.

00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:31.120
The experiment started with
a two-week control period

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:32.670
of unassisted pooping.

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:34.560
Then, participants spent another two weeks

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:35.910
using the Squatty Potty.

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:38.580
90% of the participants strained less,

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:41.453
and over 70% spent less
time on the toilet.

00:02:41.453 --> 00:02:43.244
Speaking of, we are very sorry,

00:02:43.244 --> 00:02:44.870
but put down your phone.

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:48.506
Even you, person who's watching
this on the can right now.

00:02:48.506 --> 00:02:50.660
Taking your phone or
a book to the bathroom

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:52.928
just encourages you to
stay in there longer,

00:02:52.928 --> 00:02:55.263
which, again, leads back to straining

00:02:55.263 --> 00:02:58.140
and putting excess pressure
on your rectum and anus.

00:02:58.140 --> 00:02:59.620
Getting up off the toilet can help you

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:01.440
in more ways than one.

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:04.470
Generally the more you
move, the more you poop.

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:07.222
Exercising can jostle around your innards,

00:03:07.222 --> 00:03:09.790
helping shake up food, gas, and waste

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:11.400
to move through your system.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.580
That means less time
for your lower intestine

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:15.650
to absorb water from your stool.

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:18.590
And wet, soft poops are easier to pass.

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:20.630
So going for a quick jog could be helpful

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:22.020
if you're constipated.

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:23.890
Not so much if you have diarrhea.

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:25.965
What you eat can also help.

00:03:25.965 --> 00:03:28.163
Yep, we're talking fiber.

00:03:28.163 --> 00:03:29.079
Fiber is helpful

00:03:29.079 --> 00:03:31.336
no matter which end of
the stool scale you're on,

00:03:31.336 --> 00:03:33.924
but not all fiber is created equal.

00:03:33.924 --> 00:03:35.565
There are actually two main types:

00:03:35.565 --> 00:03:37.931
soluble and insoluble.

00:03:37.931 --> 00:03:39.855
Soluble fiber dissolves in water,

00:03:39.855 --> 00:03:41.920
turning gooey and spongy.

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:43.847
It comes from things like fruit flesh,

00:03:43.847 --> 00:03:46.200
root vegetables, and cooked grains.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.540
This stuff takes its time

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:49.380
sliding through your digestive track,

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:51.280
which helps regulate movements.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:52.370
You want to start introducing

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:53.940
this type of fiber to your diet

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:56.370
if you're hovering around
a type six or seven.

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:58.290
Insoluble fiber, on the other hand,

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:00.140
mostly keeps its shape when wet.

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:02.640
This fiber from fruit skins, leafy greens,

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:04.850
and the outer layer of most whole grains

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:06.690
adds to the bulk of the stool.

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:08.460
It puts pressure on your colon walls

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:09.870
and stimulates movement.

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:11.620
So this is what you're looking for

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:13.440
to fix a type one or two,

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:14.515
but you don't want to load up

00:04:14.515 --> 00:04:16.515
on either fiber all at once.

00:04:16.515 --> 00:04:17.830
First, you want to suss out

00:04:17.830 --> 00:04:19.940
if fiber is really your issue at all.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:21.860
If you normally eat
plenty of insoluble fiber

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:23.130
but you're still constipated,

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:25.160
then more probably isn't gonna help.

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:26.772
And too much fiber too quickly

00:04:26.772 --> 00:04:29.370
can make you bloated or gassy.

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:31.692
When in doubt, go see your doctor.

00:04:31.692 --> 00:04:33.272
They might recommend probiotics,

00:04:33.272 --> 00:04:35.280
which can help reduce bloating and gas

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:37.129
as well as constipation.

00:04:37.129 --> 00:04:38.250
When you first start taking them,

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:41.170
you might end up in type
six or seven territory

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:43.650
for a few days, but that should go away.

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:45.650
And if adding stuff to
your diet doesn't help,

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:47.350
maybe try taking stuff away.

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:49.125
Dairy, caffeine, meats,

00:04:49.125 --> 00:04:51.500
spicy foods, alcohol, grease,

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:54.180
certain fruits, and artificial sweeteners

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:57.104
have all been known to cause diarrhea.

00:04:57.104 --> 00:04:59.094
Cutting all or some of that stuff

00:04:59.094 --> 00:05:02.540
could help relieve those
bowel-control issues.

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:04.399
Keeping a food diary to find connections

00:05:04.399 --> 00:05:07.557
between snacks and symptoms
is also recommended,

00:05:07.557 --> 00:05:09.170
and that way you don't have to give up

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:11.000
on all the good stuff at once.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:13.787
If you're not the world's
only perfect pooper,

00:05:13.787 --> 00:05:16.800
taking the perfect poop isn't always easy.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:20.761
But it should never be
as hard as a type one.

00:05:20.761 --> 00:05:22.700
With these tips and tricks
in your back pocket,

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:24.970
you are well on your way to the throne.

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:26.960
Now go eat, drink, and jog your way

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:29.360
to the best poop of your life.

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:31.270
You earned it, champ.

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:33.210
Everybody deserves a perfect poo,

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:35.150
but always make sure to
check with your doctor

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:36.760
before you make significant changes

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:38.580
to your diet or lifestyle.

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:40.510
But you could probably moo all you want

00:05:40.510 --> 00:05:42.351
without a doctor's note.

00:05:42.351 --> 00:05:44.309
And subscribe below if you want more ways

00:05:44.309 --> 00:05:46.193
to optimize your life with science.

